{
  "extends": "@tsconfig/svelte/tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "incremental": true,
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.tsc.tsbuildinfo",
    "target": "ES2021",
    "useDefineForClassFields": true,
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "typeRoots": ["./node_modules/@types", "../node_modules/@types"],
    /**
     * `svelte` and `vite/client` are deliberately absent from this list even though
     * `tsconfig.json` next door names all three, and this is a TypeScript 7 behaviour change
     * rather than a narrowing of what is ambient here. TS 7 resolves a `types` entry
     * against `typeRoots` only; neither of those is an `@types/*` package, so naming them
     * fails with TS2688 "Cannot find type definition file". Both still load — `env.d.ts`
     * pulls them in with `/// <reference types="..." />`, which resolves through ordinary
     * package resolution — and `--listFiles` confirms `svelte/types/index.d.ts` and
     * `vite/client.d.ts` are in this program. Do not "fix" this by adding them back.
     */
    "types": ["node"],
    "noEmit": true,
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "moduleDetection": "force",
    "paths": {
      "@shared/*": ["../shared/*"],
      "@gphone/sdk": ["./index.ts"],
      "@gphone/sdk/app": ["./app.ts"],
      "@gphone/sdk/core": ["./core.ts"]
    }
  },
  /**
   * MICA-184. The pure-TypeScript core of the package: everything that never reaches a
   * `.svelte`, held to the same TS 7 that already checks `client/` and `server/`. Root
   * drives it (`typecheck:sdk` in the root `package.json`) exactly as it drives those two —
   * the package owns its compiler options, root owns the compiler.
   *
   * **This is additive.** `sdk/tsconfig.json` is untouched and `svelte-check` still checks
   * the whole package, so nothing here can leave a file unchecked; what a file can lose is
   * this stricter pass. Narrowing `svelte-check` to match was tried and is a no-op — its
   * program is the transitive closure of the `.svelte` files, so the pure core arrives as
   * their dependencies regardless (823 files either way, and an error injected into an
   * "excluded" file is still reported).
   *
   * That was preferred to installing TS 7 into this package under an alias. The alias works
   * and keeps the bare `typescript` specifier at 6.0.3, which is what `typescript-eslint`
   * resolves and refuses to run without — but it was tried on this tree and pnpm hands the
   * aliased package's bin the same name, so `sdk/node_modules/.bin/tsc` silently became
   * 7.0.2 while `require('typescript')` stayed 6.0.3. A package whose two answers for "which
   * TypeScript" disagree is a worse trap than reaching for root's binary.
   *
   * ## The exclude list is the partition, and it is checked
   *
   * The five barrels below are the only non-test `.ts` files in this package that reach a
   * `.svelte`. Excluding a file that no longer needs to be excluded costs it TS 7 coverage
   * and **fails nothing** — and neither does the reverse, because `svelte/types` declares
   * `*.svelte` ambiently, so tsc happily types a component import as an opaque
   * `ComponentType`. `scripts/check-sdk-partition.js` is the only thing standing behind this
   * list; it recomputes the import graph on every `pnpm typecheck` and fails on any
   * disagreement in either direction. Read its header before editing this.
   *
   * The suite is excluded wholesale, as a decision rather than an omission: 30 of the 58
   * test files reach a `.svelte` and many import the barrels, and the rest reach into
   * `web/src` on purpose (the documented exception to the boundary), which would pull the
   * phone's own source into a TS 7 program and fail on errors `web/`'s own gate does not
   * raise. Measured: 10 such errors, 7 of them in files this package does not own.
   */
  "include": ["**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "**/*.test.ts",
    "index.ts",
    "addon.ts",
    "core.ts",
    "components.ts",
    "icons.ts"
  ]
}
